From bc423e2fee9a56bcbd19a8450e97c46796f86beb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: two prompts say MihawkOS, not Windows

The owner's rule of 2026-11-06: user-facing text says MihawkOS. Of Wine's own strings in the shell's DLLs (shell32, comdlg32,
comctl32, user32, Explorer, shlwapi) two said "Windows" in a sentence a person can read:

- IDS_RESTART_PROMPT: "Do you want to simulate a MihawkOS reboot?"
- IDS_SHLEXEC_NOASSOC: "There is no program configured to open this type of file."

dlls/shell32/shell32.rc and the 49 translation files (po/*.po) that carry them: the msgids change with the English (so the
translations are kept) and the translations' own "Windows" reads MihawkOS. user32's "&More Windows..." means windows,
not the system, and stays; cmd's version line is a console tool's.
